-- title:
--   A p-torsion point independent of two given ones
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field, $W$ a Weierstrass curve over $K$, and $p$ a prime with $p \neq 2$ and with $p \neq 0$ in $K$; assume the discriminant $\Delta(W)$ is non-zero. Let $(x_1,y_1)$ and $(x_2,y_2)$ be pairs of elements of $K$ satisfying the affine Weierstrass equation of $W$ and such that the division polynomial $\mathrm{pre}\Psi_p$ of $W$ vanishes at $x_1$ and at $x_2$. Then there exist $x,y \in K$ satisfying the affine equation of $W$, with $\mathrm{pre}\Psi_p$ vanishing at $x$, such that the four elements $\mathrm{indepElt}(W,p,x,x_1)$, $\mathrm{indepElt}(W,p,x_1,x)$, $\mathrm{indepElt}(W,p,x,x_2)$ and $\mathrm{indepElt}(W,p,x_2,x)$ are all non-zero, where $\mathrm{indepElt}(W,p,x_0,t) = \prod_{a=1}^{(p-1)/2}\bigl(t\,\Psi^{2}_{a}(x_0) - \Phi_a(x_0)\bigr)$, the product over $a$ in the interval $[1,(p-1)/2]$ of $t$ times the evaluation at $x_0$ of $W.\mathrm{ΨSq}\,a$ minus the evaluation at $x_0$ of $W.\Phi\,a$. Thus $t$ is an abscissa of a non-zero multiple of a point with abscissa $x_0$ precisely when this element vanishes; the four conditions express that the new point lies in neither of the two cyclic subgroups generated by the given points, and that neither of those points lies in the subgroup generated by the new one.
--
--   This is the fibrewise statement that the $p$-torsion of an elliptic curve over an algebraically closed field of residue characteristic different from $p$ contains a third cyclic subgroup beyond any two given ones, since $\#W[p](K) = p^{2}$ while the union of two cyclic subgroups of order $p$ has at most $2p-1$ elements. It is used in the construction of level-$p$ structures in the sense of Katz–Mazur, feeding [`ModularCurve.exists_isLevelPStructure_of_isAlgClosed`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_isLevelPStructure_of_isAlgClosed) and [`ModularCurve.KatzLevelPForm.existsUnique_pullbackLevelP_eq_of_swapInvariant`](thm.html#ModularCurve.KatzLevelPForm.existsUnique_pullbackLevelP_eq_of_swapInvariant).
-- source:
